[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r11
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Routing policy on r11 (FRRouting/OSPF/EIGRP), specifically the absence of a default route toward the “Internet/core.”

Mechanism: PC12 (120.1.1.10) sends traffic to its gateway r12 (120.1.1.1). r12’s default route is via r11 (default via 112.1.1.1 dev eth0). When traffic is destined outside internal prefixes, r11 has no route for it and immediately returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable,” which the user experiences as the “internet cutting out.” Internal destinations (e.g., 120.0.0.0/8) continue to work, making the problem seem intermittent.

Localization: 
- Access link pc12 ↔ r12.eth1 (120.1.1.0/8) is healthy: 0% loss over 20 pings; no RX/TX errors/drops on either end.
- Upstream: r12 forwards default to r11 (112.1.1.1). r11 runs OSPF to r1 on 111.1.1.0/8 and EIGRP to r12, but lacks a default route.

Direct evidence:
- pc12 ping 8.8.8.8 → “From 112.1.1.1 Destination Net Unreachable.”
- r12 ping 8.8.8.8 → same unreachable from 112.1.1.1.
- r11: “show ip route 0.0.0.0/0” returns no entry; OSPF adjacency to r1 is up but no default installed.

Root cause: r11 is not receiving or configured with a default route toward the core/Internet.

Corrective fix: Add a default route on r11 pointing to r1 (e.g., ip route 0.0.0.0/0 111.1.1.1) or have r1 originate a default into OSPF (router ospf; default-information originate). After adding, verify r11 installs 0/0 and confirm external reachability from r12 and pc12 (e.g., ping 8.8.8.8). No action is needed on the pc12 access port. 
=== END ===